---
import BaseHead from '../components/BaseHead.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
	<head>
		<BaseHead title="About — Content" description="About Content, an independent publication by Ken Mazaika about content systems, distribution, and AI-assisted marketing." />
		<link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com" />
		<link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin />
		<link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=DM+Sans:wght@400;500;600&family=IBM+Plex+Mono:wght@400;500&family=Libre+Caslon+Display&family=Source+Serif+4:opsz,wght@8..60,400;8..60,600&display=swap" rel="stylesheet" />
	</head>
	<body>
		<Header />
		<main class="about-page">
			<header>
				<p class="issue-line">About this publication</p>
				<h1>Content is where I study how ideas travel.</h1>
			</header>
			<div class="about-grid">
				<div class="about-statement">
					<p>I write from inside the work: building a publishing system, testing distribution, using AI agents, and trying to keep the result from sounding like it came off an assembly line.</p>
				</div>
				<div class="about-body">
					<p>The easy part of content production is increasingly the draft. The harder parts are deciding what deserves to exist, developing a point of view, checking the work, and giving an idea a native life in each place it appears.</p>
					<p>This publication documents those harder parts. Some pieces are workflows you can copy. Others are experiments, research notes, or honest postmortems on what did and did not reach an audience.</p>
					<p><strong>Ken Mazaika</strong> is an engineering leader and technical creator in Los Angeles. He uses Hermes as part of the publication’s research and production system, with a human at the editorial gate.</p>
				</div>
			</div>
		</main>
		<Footer />
	</body>
</html>
